IMPORTANT: After completing the task below, you MUST output ONLY a raw JSON object. Do NOT wrap it in markdown or add any prose — the workflow fails without it.

Work in the current working directory and complete this goal:

Act as a principal product designer specializing in macOS menu-bar utilities. Design a best-in-class information architecture and interaction model for a personal msw sandbox monitor with three workspaces: dev, playgrounds, personal. Cover the compact status-item affordance, popover layout, workspace cards, progressive disclosure, quick actions, destructive-action confirmation, loading/error/offline states, keyboard navigation, accessibility, visual semantics, notifications, and settings. Map each user need to the least-friction UI surface and explicitly avoid menu-bar clutter. Do not edit files or run project-wide tests/formatters/linters. Return a concrete UX specification with recommended labels, hierarchy, and interaction details.

Keep the change minimal and focused. Verify the work. Report a concise summary and every file changed.


**REQUIRED OUTPUT** — You MUST return ONLY a raw JSON object matching this schema:
{
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "summary": {
      "type": "string",
      "minLength": 20
    },
    "filesChanged": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
        "type": "string"
      }
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "summary",
    "filesChanged"
  ],
  "additionalProperties": false
}
Do not include prose, markdown, headings, commentary, or code fences.
The first character of your response must be `{` and the last character must be `}`.
The workflow will fail unless the entire response is the JSON object.

